<title>TURKEY: Turk Tupras 9-mth losses double.</title>
<headline>Turk Tupras 9-mth losses double.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share loss   (lira)	1,031.86  vs     491.11</p>
<p>    Loss				 4,820.87  vs   2,294.47</p>
<p>    Net sales			227,781.13  vs 114,406.59</p>
<p>    Operating loss		  13,937.25  vs   2,470.80</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	    10,275.79  vs   1,631.17</p>
<p>    Interest paid			889.50  vs   1,281.29</p>
<p>    Total debts		    112,077.65  vs  52,815.88</p>
<p>    Equity			    22,068.96  vs  16,350.59</p>
<p>    Capital			    4,672.00  vs   4,672.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's largely state-owned petroleum refiner Tupras Turkiye Petrol Rafineriler A.S. operates four refineries. It is slated for privatisation, with 96.41 percent of its capital held by the privatisation agency OIB.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
